    <title>Large Language Models for Reasoning: A Comprehensive Survey</title>
    <summary>This paper provides a comprehensive survey of large language models (LLMs)
    for reasoning tasks. We review recent advances in chain-of-thought prompting,
    instruction tuning, and retrieval augmented generation (RAG). Our analysis covers
    both theoretical foundations and practical applications across multiple domains.</summary>
